# Build an Underdark Warrior and photograph his saving throws, which is bd
# inc-tek.8.3 finding PA-03-F13: the class header and its level table both
# advertise a good Reflex save, and the class flags gave the poor track.
#
# The header at lib/prestige.irh:3038 reads Saves: *<9>FR<1>w*, so Fortitude
# and Reflex are highlighted and Will is not. The level table prints
# +2 +3 +3 +4 +4 in the Reflex column, which is GoodSave[1..5] digit for
# digit (src/Tables.cpp:100-103). The flags said only CF_GOOD_FORT, and
# src/Values.cpp:395 picks the track from that flag, so a 5th-level
# Underdark Warrior had Reflex +1 -- PoorSave[5] -- where his own page
# printed +4. The fix adds CF_GOOD_REF.
#
# THE ORACLE is the sheet's Reflex line, which names each class's own
# contribution separately: "Reflex +N (Rogue +N/ Underdark Warrior +N, ...)".
# The rogue's share is the control -- it must not move.
#
# This character also proves the ADMITTING half of PA-03-F12, the race gate
# that was never checked. A deep gnome is one of the five races the fix
# admits, and he is tested UNREDUCED: collapsing him to his parent race
# would yield the surface gnome, whom the gate must refuse. The refusing
# half is tools/keys/underdark-greyelf.keys.
#
# THE BUILD, and why every number in it is forced.
#   * Race. The gate wants drow, kobold, orc, deep gnome or grey dwarf.
#   * Wisdom 17 base. A deep gnome carries Wis +2, so 15 bought is enough.
#     Point buy is used rather than a rolled set, so the character does not
#     depend on the seed at all.
#   * Move Silently, Hide and Climb at 10. All three are rogue skills.
#   * Blind Fighting and Toughness. Toughness is the expensive one: it needs
#     Con 13 AND Endurance AND Roll With It (src/FeatTab.cpp:1237-1242), so
#     three of the four feats are spent reaching it. Two feats arrive during
#     character generation and one each at 3rd and 6th level, which is why
#     the character is a Rogue 6 and not a Rogue 5.
#   * Six core levels plus five prestige levels is exactly 11, which is
#     MAX_CHAR_LEVEL (inc/Defines.h:4367). There is no room to spare.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Gnome"
@choose "Deep Gnome"
@choose "Rogue"

# Point buy, 75 points, spent to the last one. The seven rows are the
# engine's own attribute list (src/Create.cpp:1617-1622), fixed at seven and
# in a fixed order, so counting DOWN here cannot rot the way counting
# through a list built from lib/ can.
p
RIGHT*6         # STR 14
DOWN
RIGHT*10        # DEX 18
DOWN
RIGHT*10        # CON 18, because Toughness wants a Constitution of 13 and
                #   both races here carry a penalty to it
DOWN
RIGHT*8         # INT 16
DOWN
RIGHT*7         # WIS 15, which the deep gnome's +2 turns into 17
DOWN
RIGHT*9         # CHA 17
DOWN
RIGHT*6         # LUC 14
ENTER y         # "Are these your final stats?"

@choose "Neutral"
@choose "Endurance"     # Toughness needs it
@choose "Roll With It"  # and it needs this too
@while "Choose a feat" a        # some races are given a third feat; spend it

# Eighteen ranks, two to a skill. The three the gate reads first; the rest
# only because character generation will not release a character with a rank
# unspent.
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Climb" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Alchemy" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Appraise" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Athletics" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Balance" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Bluff" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Craft" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Decipher Script" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Diplomacy" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Disguise" DOWN
RIGHT*3
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks. A high Intelligence buys more
        #   ranks, so more skills are named here than the smallest character
        #   needs; a RIGHT with no rank left to spend does nothing.

a       # Personality archetype

ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play
w       # wizard mode
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE   # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
ESC

d                       # character sheet

# Level to 3, where the third feat is offered, and to 6 for the fourth.
# Pressing G until the menu appears is safer than counting levels: it does
# not care which levels a rogue is given a feat at.
@until "Choose a feat" G
# Toughness is drawn as "[ ] Toughness": the feat list is longer than the 52
# letters LMenu has to give out, so the entries past the 52nd get a blank
# bracket. A menu ignores the space bar, so the only way in is to put the
# cursor on the row and press ENTER. DOWN walks the whole list, column by
# column, and wraps (src/TextTerm.cpp:1145-1152).
@cursorto "Toughness" DOWN
ENTER
@until "Choose a feat" G
@choose "Blind Fight"
@expect "Rogue 6"

S
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" DOWN
RIGHT*9
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" UP
RIGHT*9
@cursorto:mark "Climb" UP
RIGHT*9
ENTER y

P                       # [P]restige Classes
@expect "Choose a class:"
@choose "Underdark Warrior"
@expect "Warrior 0"     # the gate admitted him. The sheet wraps the
                        #   class name, so only the tail is looked for.

@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Underdark Warrior"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Underdark Warrior"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Underdark Warrior"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Underdark Warrior"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Underdark Warrior"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@expect "Warrior 5"

W                       # Write Dump
u d w a r ENTER         # filename: "udwar"
ESC
@quit
